The docx skill is authored by the ultrawork project. It is not derived from Anthropic's
proprietary document skills, nor from any of the third-party skill collections surveyed
in docs/discussions/059 §2 — SKILL.md, scripts, fixtures and capabilities.json are
written from scratch (see docs/discussions/059 §5 L0 for the clean-room gate that
checks this, including an AST-skeleton fingerprint that survives renaming).

It invokes the following third-party software at runtime (NOT bundled; installed by the
user per the SKILL.md instructions):
  - lxml (BSD-3-Clause)
  - LibreOffice / soffice (MPL-2.0), invoked as an external command

python-docx is deliberately NOT a dependency: the skill reads and writes
WordprocessingML through lxml directly (SKILL.md explains why). It is used by the
ultrawork repository's own gates as an independent third-party reader of the artifacts
this skill produces, which is a different role and does not travel with the skill.

The ECMA-376 element orderings encoded in scripts/office/xmlorder.py are taken from the
published standard (ECMA-376 Part 1, §17.3 / §17.4 / §17.6), which is a specification of
fact. The sample documents under fixtures/ are generated by fixtures/make_fixtures.py,
which builds every part of the package from scratch; no third-party template is used.
